 1. join returns                                         None
 2. no Thread.value: a Future's result()                 2
 3. after it ends: is_alive() / status                   False / (no status attribute)
 4. current_thread() is main_thread(): outside / inside  True / False
 5. a new thread has its own get_native_id()             True
 6. a thread did x += 1 on the outer local; x is now     11
 7. Thread(target=add, args=(1, 2)) -> result            3
 8. join returns normally; excepthook got                ValueError: boom (join returned None)
 9. is_alive() after an exception                        False
10. a waiting thread / the current thread                is_alive() True / (no status attribute)
11. time.sleep(0) is the hint; sys.getswitchinterval()   0.005
12. results through a Queue, sorted after join           [(0, 0), (1, 1), (2, 4)]
13. main ends -> child stdout: non-daemon / daemon=True  'main done\nworker done\n' / 'main done\n'
14. default excepthook -> child's stderr, line 1         'Exception in thread Thread-1 (boom):'
